>Not necessarily if you compile the console version.

You will need to make some rather icky modifications to the makefiles if
you want to cross-compile for a target which uses a different object
code format (which applies in the "Linux host, Windows target" case -
Linux uses ELF, Windows uses something else), different sizes for
standard C numeric types, or different byte ordering for multi-byte
numeric types.  The 'makedefs' program built as part of Nethack's build
process, which generates source and header files that other parts of the
build process depend on, links against object modules which are also
linked into the finished Nethack executable.

